# Wireframe: Issue Assignee Selector

## Purpose & Flow Context

The Issue Assignee Selector is a dropdown component that allows users to assign or reassign an issue to a team member. Entry: user clicks assignee avatar or "Assign" button on IssueCard or IssueDetail. Exit: user selects an assignee (optimistic update applied) or clicks outside/presses Escape (dropdown closes without change).

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Dropdown is positioned absolute relative to trigger, not part of grid layout.

**App-shell**: Dropdown overlays content, positioned below trigger element.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Trigger Button | Current assignee avatar + name + chevron, or "Unassigned" placeholder | Click opens dropdown |
| Dropdown Menu | Search input (optional), user list with avatars | Positioned below trigger, max-height with scroll |

```
+-------------------------------+
|  [👤  Sarah Chen      ▼]    |
+-------------------------------+
|  [>  Unassigned             ] |
|  [>  👤  Sarah Chen         ] |
|  [>  👤  Mike Johnson       ] |
|  [>  👤  Emily Park         ] |
|  [>  👤  Alex Rivera        ] |
+-------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Trigger Button | Button | Click opens dropdown, shows current assignee or "Unassigned" | Keyboard Enter/Space opens |
| Dropdown Menu | List | Contains user options, scrollable if many users | Max-height with scroll |
| User Option | List Item | Click selects assignee, closes dropdown | Hover highlight, keyboard arrow navigation |
| Unassigned Option | List Item | Click removes assignee | First option in list |
| User Avatar | Avatar | Shows user avatar or initials | 24px circle |
| User Name | Text | Shows user full name | Truncates if too long |

## Data Display

User options are displayed in a vertical list, sorted by:
1. Current assignee (if any) at top
2. Team members alphabetically by name
3. "Unassigned" option always available

Each option shows:
- User avatar (24px circle)
- User full name
- Active indicator (checkmark) if currently assigned

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Trigger Label | Shows current assignee | "Sarah Chen" or "Unassigned" |
| Unassigned Option | Allows removing assignment | "Unassigned", "No assignee" |
| User Name | Identifies team member | Full name, e.g. "Sarah Chen" |
| Active Indicator | Shows current selection | Checkmark icon next to assigned user |

## States

### Closed (Default)

Trigger button shows current assignee, dropdown hidden.

```
+-------------------------------+
|  [👤  Sarah Chen      ▼]    |
+-------------------------------+
```

### Open (Dropdown Visible)

Dropdown appears below trigger, showing user list.

```
+-------------------------------+
|  [👤  Sarah Chen      ▲]    |
+-------------------------------+
|  [>  Unassigned             ] |
|  [>  👤  Sarah Chen      ✓ ] |
|  [>  👤  Mike Johnson       ] |
|  [>  👤  Emily Park         ] |
|  [>  👤  Alex Rivera        ] |
+-------------------------------+
```

### Selecting (Keyboard Navigation)

User navigates options with arrow keys, current option highlighted.

```
+-------------------------------+
|  [👤  Sarah Chen      ▲]    |
+-------------------------------+
|  [>  Unassigned             ] |
|  [>  👤  Sarah Chen      ✓ ] |
|  [>  👤  Mike Johnson  ■■■ ] |  ← highlighted
|  [>  👤  Emily Park         ] |
|  [>  👤  Alex Rivera        ] |
+-------------------------------+
```

### Applied (Optimistic Update)

User selected new assignee, dropdown closes, trigger updates immediately.

```
+-------------------------------+
|  [👤  Mike Johnson    ▼]    |
+-------------------------------+
  (trigger updated, API request in background)
```

### Reverted (Update Failed)

Optimistic update failed, trigger reverts to previous assignee.

```
+-------------------------------+
|  [👤  Sarah Chen      ▼]    |
+-------------------------------+
  (trigger reverted, error toast shown)
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full dropdown with all options, positioned below trigger |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same as desktop |
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-width dropdown at bottom of screen, larger touch targets, may use native select |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | Dropdown is within main landmark |
| Heading order | No headings in dropdown |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus moves to dropdown when opened, arrow keys navigate options |
| Accessible names | Trigger: aria-label="Assign issue to", Options: aria-label="{user name}" |
| Keyboard operability | Enter/Space opens, Arrow keys navigate, Enter selects, Escape closes |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on trigger and all options |
| Focus not obscured | Dropdown doesn't obscure trigger (positioned below) |
| Non-color intent | User name + avatar, not just color |
